          <hardTeach>John 1:1–9: the Word was with God and was God; he is the true light. Romans 1:19–20: what can be known of God is plain in the things that have been made. Augustine’s illumination (De Magistro; Confessions VII) treats our seeing of truth as participation in that Light. Aquinas: the intellect is measured by being, and being is from God (ST I, q.16; q.84). Reason is not a late accident. It already leans on a ground.</hardTeach>
