        <p>Romans 2:14–15 treats that law as already shared. Augustine locates the eternal law in God; Aquinas calls natural law our share in it. This is Ansel’s gate step — not Hope’s later ridge that duty is more than taste. Nature as a pile of facts is not enough.</p>
