          <hardTeach>Acts 17:24–28: the God who made the world and everything in it does not live in temples made by hands; he gives to all life and breath and everything; in him we live and move and have our being. Augustine: our heart is restless until it rests in God (Confessions I.1). Aquinas: God is ipsum esse subsistens — not a first brick in the pile, the living source of being (ST I, q.3; q.44). Feser (secondary) traces that same classical theism for modern readers. Cosmo is only the loci guide at Why Gate Bedrock. This is the foundation beat. It is not the later first-mover or kalām walk. It is the living God under the trusts you already spend.</hardTeach>
